IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `eta-requirements`

-- Electronic Transactions Act 1999 (Cth), ss 7A, 7B, 9-12, 14, 14A, 15, 15A-15D, 17(3), Schedule 1 -- worked cases from
-- the seat of the contracting party.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked against a
-- decided case or the Electronic Transactions Regulations (not deposited). This is the Commonwealth Act; the WA Electronic
-- Transactions Act 2011 is not encoded.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_electronic-transactions-act-1999_baseline.py).
-- Expected results were written by hand from the text.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel): on 10 July 2031 Daniel's company Jarrah
-- settles standard terms for its software, with electronic acceptance, and asks "is a click acceptance?" (d045). The
-- scenario names no customer, method or governing-law clause; those are the encoder's. Priya's citizenship by conferral
-- (2030) is from the scenario; the documents are the encoder's. Fixtures not marked (d045) are invented for the case.

