§ `s 9 -- writing`

#ASSERT (`Can I meet the writing requirement electronically` `lodging a written objection with the Commissioner of Taxation (invented)` `lodged through the online service the entity requires, with its receipt step done`) EQUALS `met electronically`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the writing requirement electronically` `lodging a written objection with the Commissioner of Taxation (invented)` `emailed, although the entity requires its online service`) EQUALS `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the writing requirement electronically` `giving a customer a written notice under a Commonwealth law (invented)` `the customer clicked I agree while logged in to Jarrah's portal, which Jarrah set up (d045)`) EQUALS `met electronically`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the writing requirement electronically` `filing a document in a federal court under its rules (invented)` `lodged through the online service the entity requires, with its receipt step done`) EQUALS `the Act does not apply: court or tribunal practice and procedure (s 7B(1))`

§ `s 10 -- signature (d045: is a click acceptance?)`

-- d045: no Commonwealth law requires Jarrah's customer terms to be signed, so s 10 does not reach the click at all.
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the signature requirement electronically` `Jarrah's customer terms: no Commonwealth law requires the customer to sign them (d045)` `the customer clicked I agree while logged in to Jarrah's portal, which Jarrah set up (d045)`) EQUALS `the Act does not apply: the requirement is not under a law of the Commonwealth`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the signature requirement electronically` `a Commonwealth law requiring the customer's signature, given to Jarrah (invented, d045)` `the customer clicked I agree while logged in to Jarrah's portal, which Jarrah set up (d045)`) EQUALS `met electronically`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the signature requirement electronically` `a Commonwealth law requiring the customer's signature, given to Jarrah (invented, d045)` `an anonymous I agree click with no login`) EQUALS `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the signature requirement electronically` `a Commonwealth law requiring the customer's signature, given to Jarrah (invented, d045)` `a click whose reliability is doubted, but the login logs prove who clicked and that they meant it`) EQUALS `met electronically`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the signature requirement electronically` `a Commonwealth law requiring the customer's signature, given to Jarrah (invented, d045)` `an emailed typed name, where the recipient never agreed to take signatures that way`) EQUALS `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the signature requirement electronically` `the same signature requirement, exempted by the regulations (invented)` `the customer clicked I agree while logged in to Jarrah's portal, which Jarrah set up (d045)`) EQUALS `the Act does not apply: the regulations exempt it (s 7A)`

§ `s 11 and Schedule 1 -- production`

#ASSERT (`Can I meet the production requirement electronically` `producing a paper invoice to a Commonwealth officer on request (invented)` `a complete PDF scan, emailed in the format the officer asked for`) EQUALS `met electronically`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the production requirement electronically` `producing a paper invoice to a Commonwealth officer on request (invented)` `a phone photo missing the second page`) EQUALS `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the production requirement electronically` `producing documents for Priya's citizenship application (2030, Schedule 1)` `a complete PDF scan, emailed in the format the officer asked for`) EQUALS `the Act does not apply: a Schedule 1 migration or citizenship document (s 11(5))`

§ `s 12 -- recording and retention`

#ASSERT (`Can I meet the recording requirement electronically` `keeping Jarrah's paper records for a period under a Commonwealth tax law (invented)` `scans kept readable and unaltered in Jarrah's document system`) EQUALS `met electronically`

#ASSERT (`Can I meet the retention requirement with an electronic form` `keeping Jarrah's paper records for a period under a Commonwealth tax law (invented)` `scans kept readable and unaltered in Jarrah's document system` TRUE) EQUALS `met electronically`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the retention requirement with an electronic form` `keeping Jarrah's paper records for a period under a Commonwealth tax law (invented)` `scans kept readable and unaltered in Jarrah's document system` FALSE) EQUALS `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`

#ASSERT (`Can I meet the retention requirement for an electronic communication` `keeping Jarrah's paper records for a period under a Commonwealth tax law (invented)` `Jarrah's mailbox archive, with sender, recipient and sent and received times` TRUE) EQUALS `met electronically`
#ASSERT (`Can I meet the retention requirement for an electronic communication` `keeping Jarrah's paper records for a period under a Commonwealth tax law (invented)` `email bodies saved as text, without the headers` TRUE) EQUALS `not met electronically: a condition of the section is not satisfied`

§ `ss 14, 14A -- dispatch and receipt`

#ASSERT (`When is my communication dispatched` `Jarrah's email of its new terms to the customer's designated address, reaching it at hour 10`) EQUALS `when it left my information system`
#ASSERT (`When is my communication dispatched` `a message posted inside a portal both parties use, never leaving Jarrah's system`) EQUALS `when the addressee received it, because it never left my information system`
#ASSERT (`When is my communication dispatched` `an email under a contract term fixing its own time of receipt`) EQUALS `at the time the addressee and I agreed`

#ASSERT (`At what hour is my communication received` `Jarrah's email of its new terms to the customer's designated address, reaching it at hour 10`) EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT (`At what hour is my communication received` `the same email to a customer's other address, reaching it at hour 10, the customer aware at hour 15`) EQUALS JUST 15
#ASSERT (`At what hour is my communication received` `the same email to a customer's other address, the customer not yet aware of it`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`At what hour is my communication received` `an email under a contract term fixing its own time of receipt`) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 15 -- attribution`

#ASSERT (`Am I bound by a communication sent in my name` `an acceptance Daniel sent himself`) EQUALS `bound: I sent it, or it was sent with my authority`
#ASSERT (`Am I bound by a communication sent in my name` `an acceptance a Jarrah employee sent with Daniel's authority`) EQUALS `bound: I sent it, or it was sent with my authority`
#ASSERT (`Am I bound by a communication sent in my name` `an email sent from Daniel's account by someone who broke in`) EQUALS `not bound under s 15(1); agency law may still bind me for someone acting within actual or apparent authority`

§ `Part 2A -- contracts`

-- d045: Jarrah's terms are governed by WA law, and WA has its own equivalent (asked as a fact), so Part 2A is out.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does Part 2A apply to my contract` `Jarrah's click-through terms, governed by WA law, WA having an equivalent of Part 2A (d045)`)
#ASSERT `Does Part 2A apply to my contract` `a web-shop order under a State law with no equivalent of Part 2A (hypothetical)`
#ASSERT NOT (`Does Part 2A apply to my contract` `a web order formed in 2010, before Part 2A commenced`)

#ASSERT (`Is the online proposal an offer` `Jarrah's click-through terms, governed by WA law, WA having an equivalent of Part 2A (d045)`) EQUALS `Part 2A does not apply to this contract`
#ASSERT (`Is the online proposal an offer` `a web-shop order under a State law with no equivalent of Part 2A (hypothetical)`) EQUALS `an invitation to make offers: my order is the offer`
#ASSERT (`Is the online proposal an offer` `the same web shop, whose page clearly says it is bound when you click Buy (hypothetical)`) EQUALS `an offer: my acceptance can form the contract`

#ASSERT `Does s 15C protect my automated contract` `a web-shop order under a State law with no equivalent of Part 2A (hypothetical)`

#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my input error` `Daniel types 100 licences for 10, no confirmation screen, tells the seller at once, no use made`) EQUALS `I may withdraw the part with the error, but that alone does not end the contract`
#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my input error` `the same typo, but the seller's system showed a confirmation screen`) EQUALS `no right: the system let me correct the error`
#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my input error` `the same typo, told to the seller only a month after he noticed it`) EQUALS `no right: I did not tell the other party as soon as possible`
#ASSERT (`Can I withdraw my input error` `the same typo, after Jarrah had already used the extra licences`) EQUALS `no right: I have had material benefit from the goods or services`

